  "course": {
    "narrative": "A 41-year-old female with a long history of chronic hip and knee pain, osteoarthritis, and lumbar spondylosis presented to establish pain management care at the office. She has a history of bilateral hip and knee pain beginning in her youth, retroverted hips, degenerative disc disease, facet arthropathy, and sacroiliitis. She was previously managed by various clinics and providers, but recently had her care discontinued elsewhere due to missing an unscheduled random urine screen request. Past medical history also includes a grand mal seizure linked to past Paxil and Tramadol use, and imaging revealed a pericardial cyst. Currently, she is taking methadone, Norco, Tenormin, Skelaxin, Wellbutrin SR, and Naprosyn. On exam, she was in no acute distress with normal vitals and intact neurology. She was assessed with osteoarthritis, chronic sacroiliitis, lumbar spondylosis, migraine, TMJ arthropathy, mood disorder, and ADD. The plan includes a rheumatology referral review, bone density scan, and thyroid/parathyroid studies.",
